	select BUILTIN
	select NSH_BUILTIN_APPS
	select SCHED_WAITPID
	---help---
		Enable the CP-side bkwifi NSH command.  Besides STA connectivity and
		bounded active discovery, it can request AP-owned passive monitor and read
		aggregate metadata.  It does not expose frame transmission or raw frame
		contents.  The Wi-Fi VNET driver is owned by BK7258_WIFI_VNET and is
		enabled independently of this command.  SCHED_WAITPID keeps built-ins in
		the foreground so the interactive credential reader exclusively owns the
		NSH terminal until it has restored terminal echo.

